{
	title: 'Color themes as plugins, switched by /theme',
	spec: "Themes are plugins (task an). Each theme is a tracked file themes/<name>.ts at the repo root (outside plugins/, so the loader does not load them all), written like any plugin: it exports `look` (type Look in src/common/colors.ts: replacements for colors fields; a function field is replaced by a function given the field it replaces, a plain value (fgL, screen, mix) by a plain value) and a registration function that applies each with plugin.around or plugin.set (so removing it puts the built-in look back exactly) and redraws the terminal in plugin.onChange. The active theme is plugins/color-theme.ts in the Hal home: a relative symlink (computed between real paths) to themes/<name>.ts, so a pull that improves a theme reaches the active one after a restart; plugins/.gitignore keeps it local. No link means the built-in look in colors.ts, named hal: cyan and orange phosphor on near-black, the old Hal's hues with more contrast and punch, and no slate (borders and buttons are cyan). A theme can change every color Hal draws (task 1w: all of them, derivations included, are colors fields). themes/hal.ts writes the built-in look out in full, every colors field, derivations as functions given the field they replace first, as a template to copy to themes/<name>.ts and tweak; /theme hal still means no link (the built-in), and hal is listed once. Shipped themes: nostromo (Alien: amber text, green phosphor for you, brown-black), tron (cyan lines on black, orange Hal, cards barely tinted), wopr (WarGames: one green phosphor in several brightnesses, errors alone red), tyrell (Blade Runner: blue-black, hot pink Hal, neon cyan you, amber warnings). Every theme passes the same readable-text check as the built-in look (tasks/README.md) and follows its look (no slate, no glow). The web page picks the theme up on its next load (its color CSS is generated per page load, from the host's colors). /theme (host command, model-usable) with no argument asks a question (a choice of hal and every themes/*.ts, the active one chosen), never just prints a list; the answer, or /theme <name>, points the link at it, replacing it with one rename so the loader never sees it missing (hal removes the link); an unknown name is an error listing the choices; a color-theme.ts that is the user's own file, not a link, is never replaced (an error says so). Later (not this task): pages repaint live when the theme changes; the first-run questions offer a theme and switch it live as the answer changes.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"A symlink target is resolved from the link's real directory: on macOS /var is /private/var, so a relative target computed from the unresolved path points nowhere. /theme computes it between real paths.",
